TID-CMM permitted-use terms
===========================

These are the author's own permitted-use terms for TID-CMM. They are not an
OSI-approved open-source licence, not a Creative Commons licence and not a
dedication to the public domain. The canonical statement of them is
https://tid-cmm.com/licence/ ; if this file and that page ever differ, the page
governs.

They apply to model 1.6.0, documents v1.6, the current site, and the contents of
this repository from the commit that introduces this file onward. Material
published under an earlier licence keeps it: see "Earlier versions" below.

Copyright (c) 2022-2026 Reza Adineh. All rights reserved except as expressly
permitted below.


TID-CMM is free to use under the permissions stated here. Free to use does not
mean open source, public domain, or permission to redistribute, rebrand or
create derivative products.


Permitted without written permission
------------------------------------
  - Reading, studying and citing TID-CMM.
  - Using the official assessment tool to assess your own organisation.
  - Using the official tool in paid engagements - consulting and MSSP assessment
    work included. This is expressly permitted and needs no licence.
  - Sharing the assessment reports you produce for the organisation you assessed.
  - Quoting reasonable excerpts for research, education, review and commentary,
    with attribution.
  - Linking to https://tid-cmm.com and to this repository.

Requires written permission
---------------------------
  - Republishing or redistributing the complete model, the datasets, the
    workbooks or the assessment implementation.
  - Publishing a modified or derivative version of TID-CMM.
  - Embedding the model, the scoring specification or the datasets in another
    commercial software product.
  - Rebranding, white-labelling or reselling the model or the tool.
  - Redistributing the offline assessment tool.
  - Removing TID-CMM or Reza Adineh attribution.
  - Representing an unofficial derivative as TID-CMM.
  - Using the implementation as the basis of competing derivative tooling.

Ask, and say what you want to do with it: hello@tid-cmm.com


Copyright
---------
Copyright subsists in the expression of this work: the eight domains and their
weights, the 58 sub-capabilities, all 348 level descriptors, the evidence
criteria, the five integrity constraints, the Validated Coverage Score, the
Scenario Coverage Score, the telemetry assurance method, the crosswalks, the
derived datasets, the documentation, and the assessment and site implementation.

The assessment and site implementation - the browser tool, the offline
single-file build, the workbooks and the site's own code and styles - is
copyright, all rights reserved. It is free to use as stated above; it is not
open-source licensed, and its source is not published in this repository.


Earlier versions keep the licence they were released under
----------------------------------------------------------
Model 1.5.0 and documents v1.4 were published under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0). Copies distributed under that
licence remain under it, and nothing in this file withdraws a permission already
granted for material already distributed. The terms above apply to model 1.6.0,
documents v1.6 and the current site.


